": null}, {"t_ms": 418016, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013qcKZsLnzs2z9GWcVfDxVt", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_not_found", "compensate_unknown_partial", "safe_retry_with_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 418016, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013qcKZsLnzs2z9GWcVfDxVt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 422272, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why the test failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory system, so I took \"banker's rounding\" from your request, the code's own description and the test.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018D2TXEhmSSwjiB8W4FWHuT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FvsReBDaugqYPaJLstZJ81", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01C82J5k6JEe