_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so 2.665 rounds to 2.66.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why the test failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory system, so I took \"banker's rounding\" from your request, the code's own description and the test.", "type": "text"}]}]}